load @term/seed/code/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# A hyperplane: a flat subspace one dimension below the whole, a line in the plane, a plane in space, the mirror a
# reflection fixes. The reflections in hyperplanes generate the Coxeter and Weyl groups, and the hyperplanes
# perpendicular to the roots of D4 are the mirrors whose reflections build the symmetry of the 24-cell and tile the
# mesh. The form carries the vector space the hyperplane divides.
form hyperplane
  link space, like vector-space
